# In the paraxial equation a tilted beam advances sideways by z sin(angle), not z tan(angle): 8.72 against 8.75 um here.
# Reference: z sin(angle), the paraxial result.
title Gaussian beam tilted by 5 degrees
grid dx=0.05 dz=0.125
window width=80 length=100
launch gaussian x=0 radius=3 tilt=5
plane end z=100
expect total end 0.999999919 2e-7
expect centroid end 8.7132818 2e-6
expect radius end 11.7721289 2e-6
expect neff 1.441469018 2e-8
expect centroid end 8.71557 0.02
expect radius end 11.77769 0.04
